@page "/customization/rtl-languages"
@using MudShadcn.Showcase.Pages.Customization.Examples

<DocsPage>
    <DocsPageHeader Title="RTL Languages"
                    SubTitle="Right-to-left layouts, for languages such as Arabic and Hebrew: MudBlazor's MudRTLProvider, in the shadcn look." />
    <DocsPageContent>
        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Explanation">
                <Description>
                    Right-to-left script is used in languages like Arabic and Hebrew, where writing starts at the right of the page and
                    continues to the left, so the interface has to be mirrored horizontally. MudBlazor mirrors its components inside a
                    <CodeInline>MudRTLProvider</CodeInline>, and MudShadcn styles what MudBlazor renders, so nothing else is needed.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
                To see a component that way, use the <MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.FormatTextdirectionRToL" Size="Size.Small" Style="vertical-align:text-bottom" />
                button in the top bar: it switches every page of this site, and every example on it, between left-to-right and right-to-left.
            </MudText>
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="MudRTLProvider">
                <Description>
                    Wrap the layout in a <CodeInline>MudRTLProvider</CodeInline> and put <CodeInline>MudShadcnProvider</CodeInline> inside
                    it: it holds MudBlazor's theme, popover, dialog and snackbar providers, which take their direction from the
                    <CodeInline>MudRTLProvider</CodeInline> around them. Your <CodeInline>MainLayout.razor</CodeInline> looks something like this.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent Code="@nameof(RtlProviderExample)" />
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Example">
                <Description>
                    <CodeInline>RightToLeft="true"</CodeInline> changes the layout to right-to-left. It can change while the app runs, and a
                    <CodeInline>MudRTLProvider</CodeInline> can also wrap a part of a page.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent DarkenBackground="true" Code="@nameof(RtlCardExample)" ShowCode="false" Block="true">
                <RtlCardExample />
            </SectionContent>
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Text Fields">
                <Description>
                    Text fields with <CodeInline>InputType.Email</CodeInline> or <CodeInline>InputType.Telephone</CodeInline> remain
                    left-aligned, with the label remaining right-aligned.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent Code="@nameof(RtlTextFieldExample)" ShowCode="false">
                <RtlTextFieldExample />
            </SectionContent>
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Border Radius">
                <Description>
                    If your application supports both left-to-right and right-to-left languages, use the <CodeInline>start</CodeInline>
                    and <CodeInline>end</CodeInline> border radius classes instead of <CodeInline>left</CodeInline> and
                    <CodeInline>right</CodeInline>. Some components, such as <MudLink Href="components/drawer">MudDrawer</MudLink>, have
                    <CodeInline>Start</CodeInline> and <CodeInline>End</CodeInline> values too.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent DarkenBackground="true" Code="@nameof(RtlBorderRadiusExample)" ShowCode="false">
                <RtlBorderRadiusExample />
            </SectionContent>
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Other useful CSS classes" />
            <ul class="docs-list">
                <li><CodeInline>.mud-flip-x-rtl</CodeInline> flips the element horizontally in right-to-left mode (for icons that should point the other way).</li>
                <li><CodeInline>.mud-rtl</CodeInline> and <CodeInline>.mud-ltr</CodeInline> give one element right-to-left or left-to-right styling.</li>
                <li>Margin and padding classes with <CodeInline>s</CodeInline> and <CodeInline>e</CodeInline> (<CodeInline>ms-4</CodeInline>, <CodeInline>pe-2</CodeInline>) follow the direction. See MudBlazor's <MudLink Href="https://mudblazor.com/utilities/spacing" Target="_blank">Spacing</MudLink> page.</li>
            </ul>
        </DocsPageSection>
    </DocsPageContent>
</DocsPage>
